  "user": "Please look up transaction TX-0401 in my account records and verify its amount. Then explain which reason codes could apply; I have not yet told you what happened.",
  "answer": "I found TX-0401 and verified its amount:\n\n- **Transaction:** TX-0401\n- **Date:** 2026-07-20\n- **Merchant:** TechMart Online\n- **Amount:** EUR 240.00 (debit, card payment)\n- **Status:** Settled\n\nI also see a second transaction, **TX-0402**, dated 2026-07-14, for EUR 240.00 at the same merchant, TechMart Online, also settled. Identical amounts at the same merchant six days apart may be relevant to your situation.\n\nBased on what this transaction is, these reason codes could apply. Which one fits depends on what happened:\n\n1. **duplicate_charge**: You were charged more than once for the same purchase. This fits if TX-0401 and TX-0402 are two charges for one order.\n2. **unauthorized_debit**: You did not authorize this payment at all.\n3. **fraud_card_not_present**: The card was used online without your involvement, for example by someone who obtained your card details.\n4. **goods_not_received**: You paid for something and did not receive it.\n5. **service_not_rendered**: You paid for a service that was not provided.\n\nPlease tell me what happened and I can check whether a dispute is eligible under the matching code. I have not opened anything. If you want to dispute, I will check eligibility first and tell you the result before any dispute is filed.",
